          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #MonoidalMonad.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %br/
              A
              %strong monoidal monad
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functors
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+natural+transformation"} monoidal transformations
          %p
            This notion originates inside the statement of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Kock70"} Kock 1970, Thm. 3.2
          %p#InComponents
            In components, this means (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kock70"} Kock 1970, p. 8
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Seal12"} Seal 2012, §1.2
          %p
            Monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
