          %p
          #cf.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Given monoidal monads
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad#the_bicategory_of_monads"} morphism of monads
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon S\Rightarrow T
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong monad
              structures (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrengthFromMonoidalness"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+natural+transformation"} monoidal natural transformation
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#support"} FPR (2019), Prop. C.5
          %p This relation has a converse:
          %p
          #BijectSymmMonoidalMonadsWithCommStrongMonads.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %br/
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              on (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of) a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              of:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monad"} commutative
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong monad
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
            %p
              and furthermore, in a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+equivalence"} logical equivalence
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properties"} properties
              of:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  being a
                  %em symmetric
                  strength in the sense of remark
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricStrength"}
              %li
                %p
                  being a
                  %em symmetric
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+monad"} monoidal monad
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalMonad"}
            %p
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kock72"} Kock (1972)
            %a{:href => "#GLLN08"} GLLN08, §7.3, §A.4
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
            formalisation is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#1Lab"} 1Lab
          %p
            Note that being a symmetric monoidal monad is a non-trivial property: see (
            %a{:href => "#McDermottUustalu22"}> McDermott &amp; Uustalu 2022, appendix A.2
            ) or
            %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/4877915/501886"} math.SE.a/4877915
            for an explicit example of a non-symmetric monoidal monad.
